All six fixes, in order: in shapes.py, `rect_area` multiplied width and height instead of adding them; in strings.py, `slugify` now splits on any run of whitespace and joins with `-` (so multiple spaces don't yield double hyphens), and `truncate` keeps only `limit - 3` characters before appending the ellipsis so the result never exceeds `limit`; in numbers_util.py, `clamp` was missing its upper bound and now also returns `high` when the value exceeds it; in dates.py, `is_leap` implements the full Gregorian rule (divisible by 4, except centuries unless divisible by 400 — so 1900 is not a leap year), and `quarter` uses `(month + 2) // 3` so months 1–3 map to quarter 1 and month 11 to quarter 4. `python check.py` now prints ALL OK.
